{% comment %}
  Outlight Ads Console Privacy Policy
  Assign this template to a page with handle "pinterest-app-privacy" in Shopify admin.
{% endcomment %}

<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 py-16 md:py-24">
  <h1 class="font-heading text-3xl md:text-4xl font-[300] text-[#131314] mb-3">Outlight Ads Console Privacy Policy</h1>
  <p class="font-body text-xs font-[300] text-[#2d3338]/60 mb-10">Last updated: April 6, 2026</p>

  <div class="landing-privacy font-body text-sm md:text-base font-[300] text-[#2d3338] leading-relaxed">
    <p class="mb-8">This Privacy Policy explains how Outlight collects, uses, stores, and protects information in connection with Outlight Ads Console, an internal tool used by authorized Outlight employees to manage and report on Outlight's own advertising operations.</p>

    <h2>Who we are</h2>
    <p>Outlight operates Outlight Ads Console. If you have questions about this policy, contact <a href="mailto:support@outlight.us">support@outlight.us</a>.</p>

    <h2>Who this app is for</h2>
    <p>Outlight Ads Console is an internal business tool. It is not available for general public use and is intended only for authorized Outlight personnel.</p>

    <h2>Information we collect</h2>
    <p>In connection with the app, we may collect and process:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Account identifiers and business profile information</li>
      <li>Advertising account, campaign, ad group, ad, creative, and reporting data</li>
      <li>Performance metrics and analytics related to Outlight's own advertiser account</li>
      <li>Technical logs, audit records, and operational events</li>
      <li>Employee authentication data used to control access to the app</li>
      <li>Related commerce and product information needed for internal reporting and campaign operations</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>How we use information</h2>
    <p>We use information to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Provide internal reporting and campaign management functionality</li>
      <li>Support approvals, audit logging, troubleshooting, and security</li>
      <li>Evaluate advertising performance for Outlight's own operations</li>
      <li>Maintain and improve the reliability of the tool</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Authorized access only</h2>
    <p>The app accesses advertising data only through authorized API credentials and approved account access. Outlight does not collect Pinterest passwords from users.</p>

    <h2>How we share information</h2>
    <p>Outlight does not sell Pinterest API data.</p>
    <p>Outlight does not share Pinterest API data with third-party advertising networks.</p>
    <p>Outlight does not use Pinterest API data for advertising outside Pinterest.</p>
    <p>Outlight may share information with service providers that support hosting, infrastructure, authentication, logging, and security, solely as needed to operate the tool.</p>

    <h2>Data retention</h2>
    <p>Outlight retains information only as long as reasonably necessary for internal reporting, operational history, security, compliance, and legitimate business purposes.</p>

    <h2>Security</h2>
    <p>Outlight uses reasonable technical and organizational safeguards to protect information, including access controls, logging, and restricted internal access.</p>

    <h2>Third-party services</h2>
    <p>The app may rely on service providers such as hosting, authentication, analytics, and ecommerce infrastructure providers. Those providers process data only as needed to support operation of the tool.</p>

    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>This tool is not intended for children under 13.</p>

    <h2>Your rights and contact</h2>
    <p>To ask questions about this policy or request information about data handling, contact <a href="mailto:support@outlight.us">support@outlight.us</a>.</p>
  </div>
</div>

